        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-25T15:08:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As discussed on GVC, the current implementation is different: we are adding to the manifest not only the toplevel libraries, but the whole top of tree up to (and including) each shared library node. So, if the top-level node is not a shared library, we descend into the children.\n\nThe current *behavior* though is the same as if we used top-level libraries, because I\u0027m not aware of any cases that would exhibit the difference (except for the tests, but they are artificial and can be fixed).\n\nI realized that the current logic doesn\u0027t make sense, because if we flatten some part of the tree and write it as a sequence of tags in the manifest, then PackageManager won\u0027t be able to unflatten it back (information will be lost). So, it will reconstruct a different run-time CLC that the build-time CLC that is used for dexpreopt and stored in the *.odex file. So if there is a practical case that exhibits the difference, we certainly don\u0027t want the current behavior, because it will cause runtime CLC mismatch and then dexpreopt is useless.\n\nI added https://r.android.com/1511271 to fix this.",
      "parentUuid": "fd2771b1_9d9da825",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 73,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 73,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "b98dd0d869c1e4e6ec2a8c2e775be82b17c416b4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
